---
title: M-Ranked — cache invalidation sequence
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant W as Collector / Analytics writer
    participant PG as PostgreSQL
    participant R as Redis
    participant A as Spring API
    participant L1 as Caffeine L1
    participant N as Next.js
    participant C as Browser / CDN

    rect rgb(232, 245, 233)
        W->>PG: BEGIN&#59; write observations/projections
        W->>PG: INSERT dataset_revision and outbox event
        W->>PG: COMMIT
        PG-->>W: committed revision R42
        W->>R: SET current_revision=R42 and PUBLISH revision.changed
        R-->>A: revision.changed(R42, affected tags)
        A->>L1: invalidate affected local entries
        A->>N: authenticated revalidate tags request
        N->>N: mark affected route/data cache stale
        Note over R: L2 values with old revision are not deleted synchronously&#59;<br/>they become unreachable and expire by bounded TTL.
    end

    rect rgb(227, 242, 253)
        C->>N: GET institution page
        N->>A: GET /api/v1/institutions/{id}
        A->>R: GET current_revision
        R-->>A: R42
        A->>L1: GET institution:R42:queryHash
        alt L1 hit
            L1-->>A: response
        else L1 miss
            A->>R: GET institution:R42:queryHash
            alt L2 hit
                R-->>A: response
                A->>L1: PUT bounded local entry
            else L2 miss
                A->>PG: SELECT published projection at R42
                PG-->>A: response rows
                A->>R: SET response with TTL
                A->>L1: PUT response
            end
        end
        A-->>N: JSON + ETag(dataset R42)
        N-->>C: HTML/RSC + Cache-Control + ETag
    end

    opt Pub/Sub event lost
        A->>R: periodic revision check
        A->>PG: fallback authoritative revision check
        Note over A,L1: New revision changes cache key&#59; stale L1 is cleared on mismatch.
    end

    Note over A,C: Admin, authentication, health and unbounded exports use no-store.